{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Dressing the Part"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "When an Interview is a Nightmare"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future with Will, Going to and the Present Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different ways to talk about the future - you can use the <span class=\"strong\">modal verb will</span>, the structure <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span> or the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous tense</span>. Each of these elements has its own use. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Refer to the chart for an outline of the use and the structure of each of these: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future or make predictions about the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ll </span>have to think of a good answer for that one for the future.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be Going To\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you talk about intentions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m going to</span> make sure I do a lot more research before my next interview.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">And I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m updating</span> the phone numbers of my references tonight!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to make sure I do a lot more research before my next interview. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll read everything I can find on the company website.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll think about answers to those tough questions!  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm updating the phone numbers of my references tonight!"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to talk about the future and you want to refer to an action that <span class=\"underline\">will be in progress at a certain time</span> in the future, you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous tense</span>. <br> You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect tense </span> to talk about something that <span class=\"underline\">be complete by a certain time </span> in the future. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> structure: <br>will (not) + be + verb-ing <br>  For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Next week, I <span class=\"strong\">will be going</span> to an interview for a freelance journalist position.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> structure: <br> will + have + past participle<br>For example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will have been</span> to four different interviews in two weeks, but no luck so far. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Next week, I will be going to an interview for a freelance journalist position. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Tomorrow, I will be thinking of you doing your presentation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "On Friday, my sister will be applying for a job in the same company."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will have been to four different interviews in two weeks, but no luck so far. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "By next week, we will have come up with a better name for the project."}, {"type": "example", "content": "By the end of the month, the company will have hired 10 new employees."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be scheduled"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be planned to start at a certain time "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The interview was scheduled for 14:00, which in international time is 2:00 p.m. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about a bad interview experience."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ordeal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very difficult process"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What an ordeal. It was a nightmare interview!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "airline industry "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "business related to building and flying airplanes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The interview was for a job in marketing in the airline industry."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "COO"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Chief Operating Officer, a high-ranking person responsible for the daily activities of a company"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  During the interview, the COO asked me a lot of unusual questions I wasn't prepared for."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mission statement"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short description of a company's purpose and goals"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He also asked me what I thought about the company mission statement, which I didn't know."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talk to 2-3 people about bad interview experiences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down the reasons why they were bad experiences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go online. Find more bad interview experiences to get ideas."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the ideas to make up an original interview experience. Write 80-100 word describing what happened."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the words <span class=\"italic\">terrible</span>, <span class=\"italic\">nightmare</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ordeal</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your text to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about interview experiences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read about other interview experiences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a text describing a negative interview experience using appropriate vocabulary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my text with a partner."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le13ob10re1img01.jpg"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instru